# _registry.ts is a flat list of one-line re-exports whose ORDER CARRIES NO MEANING (the change log
# is sorted by each entry's date+time in entries/index.ts, not by this file). Two PRs each adding a
# line is the normal case and the lines are never the same, so taking BOTH sides is always the right
# answer — which is exactly what a union merge does, with no human in the loop.
#
# Sorting the file by id already scatters insertions so most pairs don't collide at all; this catches
# the rest. Together they close the last shared-line conflict in the changelog.
#
# Do NOT extend this to structured files. A union merge on the old entries.ts — a nested array of
# objects — would have interleaved two entries' braces and produced TypeScript that doesn't compile;
# git fuses the shared `{` and `},` and union would keep both halves of the fusion. Union is only
# safe for a flat, append-only, order-independent list, which is the whole reason _registry.ts is
# shaped like one.
web/lib/changelog/entries/_registry.ts merge=union

# The runner BUNDLE must be byte-identical to what is committed, on every checkout and every
# platform. The app serves these files straight off disk and the build id is a SHA-256 over their
# raw bytes (web/lib/runner/bundle.ts), which the agent recomputes over its own copy to answer "am I
# up to date?". With core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout, git materialised all 98 of them with
# CRLF while storing LF — so the served bytes were a property of the working tree rather than of the
# commit. Any tool that wrote a file with LF (a script, a formatter, an editor) changed the build id
# without changing the code, and the next `git checkout` changed it back. The fleet was told to
# self-update either way, and a self-update EXITS the runner process.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to what is committed, so the build id is reproducible from the commit
# alone — the same on this box, in CI, and on a Linux host. Nothing here is Windows-line-ending
# sensitive: PowerShell, Node and JSON all read LF natively.
runner/** text eol=lf
